WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.070
Good morning Hank, it's Wednesday.

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:05.230
So last week was one of the worst weeks of
my life: Henry was really super-sick and we

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.450
were very scared and also he was crying all
night every night so we were staying up all

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.559
night and it was just ... misery.

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:14.190
Plus I was worried the Project for Awesome
wouldn't raise any money and the website would

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.460
break and it would be a total failure and
all of nerdfighteria would hate us and exile

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.859
us to the island of Elba.

00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:22.470
Like you know how the world's largest ball
of stamps is in Omaha, Nebraska? Well, last

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:26.759
week it felt like the world's largest ball
of suck was here, at my house.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:31.050
But then things startet to change. First and
most importantly, Henry got better. Then the

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:38.649
Project for Awesome generated more than 3,000
P4A videos and raised more than 135,000 $. It

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:42.300
probably raised much more than that, but that's
how much we can confirm. I mean, Hank, I'm

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.280
pretty sure that 135,000 $ is a lot of money,
although admittedly I'm not a mathematician.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.140
I have an idea. I'm calling Brotherhood 2.0
Resident Mathematician and State Representative

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.949
of elect Daniel Biss. (on the phone) So here's
what I wanna ask today: In your opinion as

00:00:54.949 --> 00:00:59.219
a professional mathematician who has been
published in the annals of mathematics, is

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:04.460
135,000 $ a lot of money? (after Daniel said
"Yes") Yes! We did it!

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.990
So we raised a lot of money and then, then,
then, I was on Jeopardy. So made-of-awesome

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:12.060
nerdfighter librarian named Julia Carlis was
on Jeopardy yesterday and she did not know

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.840
the question for final Jeopardy. So calmly
and confidently she wrote on her little tablet:

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.740
"Who is John Green?" as a subtle shout-out
to nerdfighteria. Which, in turn, Hank, led

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:28.100
to Alex Trebek uttering the immortal words:
"John Green, that's gonna cost you!" Julia

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:32.030
Carlis, I'm sorry that you lost on Jeopardy,
but thank you for making my life. And the

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:37.369
good news is: You win the non-existent nerdfighter-prize
of the day, which isn't nothing. Actually,

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:38.440
it is nothing.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.180
Nerdfighters, thank you for making P4A videos,
for donating, for commenting, for making Alex

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.310
Trebek say my name on television.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.189
Hank, my week has taken such a turn that I
can only share with you my happy dance as

00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:49.549
coached by wheezywaiter.

00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:53.390
Wheezywaiter: Keep dancing; don't stop.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:58.770
John: This is going to be hard.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.630
Wheezywaiter: Whoa! That wasn't very good.
That's good; you're doing good. Keep it up!

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:02.730
You're doing well. Keep it up. There you go.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:03.730
John: I'll meet you guys downstairs.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:04.730
Wheezy: That's right, keep it up. You can
do it.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:16.340
John: And now, for my grand finale, a handstand!

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:36.000
Wheezy: Ahh, that about does it. Boy, am I
tired from all the dancing.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:44.070
So Hank, on Dec 26th we're gonna draw the
raffles, eh, I've got to finish my Zombie

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:48.520
Apocalypse Novella, but I'm on it. Hank, I
will not see you on Friday, because it's Christmas

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.930
Eve, but have a wonderful holiday and I will
see you again on Monday.

